   "front": "Describe the pupillary light reflex pathway.",
   "back": "The afferent limb is the optic nerve. Fibres reach the pretectal area, which projects to the Edinger-Westphal nucleus. Preganglionic parasympathetic fibres travel in cranial nerve III to the ciliary ganglion, and postganglionic fibres innervate the pupillary constrictor muscle. Because the pretectal projections are bilateral, light in one eye constricts both pupils."
